# Switch Context

## Section

Keep two saved conversation lanes in one Session. Select one lane, ask a
question, then select the other lane and ask again. Change `backend` to
`:live` and set `OPENAI_API_KEY` to use the same Agent with a real model.

## Install this checkout

```elixir
jido_ai = Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:jido_ai, path: jido_ai},
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("../jido", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_action, path: Path.expand("../jido_action", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_signal, path: Path.expand("../jido_signal", jido_ai), override: true}
])
```

## Choose the model service

```elixir
backend = :mock

if backend == :live and is_nil(System.get_env("OPENAI_API_KEY")) do
  raise "Set OPENAI_API_KEY before you select :live"
end

script = [
  %{reply: {:text, "ALPHA is the active case."}},
  %{reply: {:text, "BETA is the active case."}}
]

mock = if backend == :mock, do: elem(Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.start_link(script: script), 1)
context = if mock, do: %{ai: %{assistant: %{options: Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.options(mock)}}}, else: %{}
```

## Define one Agent with memory

```elixir
defmodule Guide.SwitchContext do
  use Jido.AI.Agent, name: "guide_switch_context"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{
      answer: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default(""),
      messages: Jido.AI.Thread.Projection.schema()
    })

    ai :assistant do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      instructions "Answer from the selected case Context."
      reasoning :react
      memory history: :messages

      controls do
        timeout 10_000
        max_model_calls 1
      end

      result into: :answer
    end
  end

  routes do
    route "guides.ai.switch_context", ai: :assistant
  end
end
```

## Build two portable Threads

These are completed conversation data, not running requests. The public
projection validates each message before it enters a Thread.

```elixir
make_thread = fn code ->
  thread = Jido.Thread.new(metadata: %{system_prompt: "Use the saved case facts."})

  {:ok, thread} =
    Jido.AI.Thread.Projection.append(thread, [
      ReqLLM.Context.user("The case code is #{code}."),
      ReqLLM.Context.assistant("I will use #{code}.")
    ])

  thread
end

alpha = make_thread.("ALPHA")
beta = make_thread.("BETA")
```

## Select each lane and ask

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(Guide.SwitchContext, id: "guide-switch-context")

{:ok, _} =
  Jido.AI.Orchestration.modify_context(server,
    %{type: :replace, result_context: alpha},
    context_ref: "alpha",
    op_id: "load-alpha"
  )

{:ok, _} =
  Jido.AI.Orchestration.modify_context(server,
    %{type: :replace, result_context: beta},
    context_ref: "beta",
    op_id: "load-beta"
  )

{:ok, _} =
  Jido.AI.Orchestration.modify_context(server,
    %{type: :switch},
    context_ref: "alpha",
    op_id: "select-alpha"
  )

{:ok, alpha_answer} = Guide.SwitchContext.ask_sync(server, "Which case is active?", context: context)

{:ok, _} =
  Jido.AI.Orchestration.modify_context(server,
    %{type: :switch},
    context_ref: "beta",
    op_id: "select-beta"
  )

{:ok, beta_answer} = Guide.SwitchContext.ask_sync(server, "Which case is active?", context: context)

%{alpha: alpha_answer, beta: beta_answer}
```

Mock mode checks that each model request used its selected case. A switch
changes selected Context; it does not start another AgentServer.

```elixir
if mock do
  %{remaining: [], unexpected: [], requests: [first, second]} =
    Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.report(mock)

  true = String.contains?(Jason.encode!(first.body), "ALPHA")
  true = String.contains?(Jason.encode!(second.body), "BETA")
end
```

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(server)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Read [Multiple Contexts](../v3/19_multiple_contexts.md).
